%I A394738 #13 Oct 12 2026 14:33:45
%S A394738 184,459,1375,1536,6655,14739,24334
%N A394738 Numbers k such that sigma(k) = psi(k) + tau(k) + Omega(k)^3.
%C A394738 The sequence is complete. Put L := Omega(k). For every nonsquarefree k with L >= 5, one has sigma(k) - psi(k) - tau(k) >= 2^(L-1) - L - 2. Since solutions require this difference to equal L^3, we obtain L <= 11. Checking the remaining prime-exponent patterns leaves only k = p^3*q, where p and q are distinct primes satisfying (p+1)*(q+1) = 72, giving six solutions, and k = 2^9*3 = 1536. Thus the sequence consists of exactly the seven listed terms. - _Max Alekseyev_, Oct 11 2026
%e A394738 184 is a term since sigma(184) = 360 = 288 + 8 + 4^3 = psi(184) + tau(184) + Omega(184)^3.
%o A394738 (PARI) isok(k) = {my(f = factor(k)); sigma(f) == prod(i=1, #f~, (f[i, 1]+1) * f[i, 1]^(f[i, 2]-1)) + numdiv(f) + bigomega(f)^3; } \\ _Amiram Eldar_, Mar 30 2026
